Environments & Approvals in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how environments and approvals add control and safety to deployment workflows.

🔹 Environments
Environments represent deployment stages like:
Dev
Staging
Production
They help manage environment-specific rules and secrets.

🔹 Manual Approvals
Manual approvals:
Require human confirmation
Prevent accidental deployments
Add checkpoints for critical stages
Useful for production releases.

🔹 Deployment Protection
Deployment protection includes:
Approval rules
Environment-specific secrets
Access restrictions
This ensures safe and controlled deployments.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Environments add control.
 Approvals prevent mistakes.
 Protection secures releases.
